    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a concentrated attack, led by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who carries our highest efficiency score of 67.73. Facing a middling 3.92 xERA from Gray, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable right-handed platoon edge (+14%) and the premium protection of the #3 spot in the lineup, making him the anchor of our Roto production today. While **Jackson Merrill** (57.82) and **Sam Antonacci** (56.09) lack the elite upside of a top-tier matchup, both provide stable floors. **Jackson Merrill** manages to stay relevant against Gausman despite a challenging SP skill factor, largely buoyed by a strong platoon boost, while **Sam Antonacci** capitalizes on his leadoff positioning to maximize his potential for Runs and SBs, our most critical scarcity categories.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved balancing the upside of **Miguel Vargas** (48.50) against the marginal utility of **Drake Baldwin** (46.71). Ultimately, **Miguel Vargas** earns the start at 3B because his underlying xwOBA (.378) provides a safer cushion against Brown than **Drake Baldwin** faces against the elite 2.92 xERA of S\u00e1nchez. While **Drake Baldwin** is in a decent spot hitting second, the sharp drop in expected production against a sub-3.00 xERA pitcher creates a narrow margin for error. We are currently navigating a depleted roster, with **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** all idle due to team off-days, and **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining sidelined on the IL, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active bats like **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** to bridge the gap as we push for volume in the final stages of the season. \n\nWe are monitoring the weather closely, as there is latent risk for shifts in park factors that could further compress the scoring of **Drake Baldwin** and **Miguel Vargas**. With the absence of speed-threats like **Nasim Nunez** and **Wade Meckler** in the starting five today, our SB ceiling is anchored almost entirely to **Sam Antonacci** and **Jackson Merrill**. Should the late-afternoon lineups reveal any defensive shifts or lineup drops for **Heliot Ramos** or **Coby Mayo**, we may need to rotate in **Dominic Smith** or **Brayan Rocchio** to maintain our efficiency targets. For now, the focus remains on minimizing wasted game caps while squeezing every point of value out of **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Lara**, **Franklin Arias**, and **Henry Bolte** where platoon matchups allow.",
